TennisComp (the "Software") was developed by the TennisComp student project team
(GitHub: melbMinhQuan, Ejalyna, Xt162, Merryleang and zhe3364) for the Waverley Tennis
Association (the "Client").

1. Ownership

   As agreed between the team and the Client, on handover the team transfers to the
   Client all copyright and other intellectual property rights in the Software,
   including its source code, documentation, database schema and test data. The
   Client may use, copy, modify, publish, distribute, sublicense and sell the
   Software, and let others do so, without restriction and without payment to the
   team.

2. Third-party software

   The Software depends on open-source packages that remain under their own
   licences, mostly MIT, Apache-2.0, ISC and BSD. They are listed in the
   package.json files and package-lock.json, and summarised in README.md under
   "Licence and third-party software". Nothing in this file changes those
   licences, and anyone who distributes the Software must keep their notices.

3. Name and logo

   The Waverley Tennis name and logo (frontend/resources/Logo.png) belong to the
   Client.

4. No warranty

   The Software is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, express or
   implied, including the warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular
   purpose and non-infringement. In no event shall the team be liable for any
   claim, damages or other liability arising from the Software or its use.
